{
  "text": "Good morning, and welcome to the Northwind Harbor Weather and Traffic Report for Tuesday, March 14th. My name is Sarah Johnson, and with me in the studio is Dr. Miguel Alvarez. Today the temperature in Seattle reached 72 degrees, while Portland recorded 68. The Aurora Bridge reopened at 6:45 this morning after repairs that cost $1.2 million dollars. About 38,000 drivers cross it every day. At the airport, Flight 417 from Chicago landed 25 minutes early, and Gate B12 is now open. Tomorrow we expect heavy rain beginning around 3 in the afternoon, with winds of 25 miles per hour. Thank you for listening.",
